From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:12:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 17/47] r4 journey fix 2: journey lakeside sun = the board's
 sun in the lake frame (one source, lakesideSunForward)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The journey mounts the r5h3 scene turned by lakesideJourney().yawDeg (180°) but
slerped the main light to the unturned sunForward, so the light was mirrored
against the lake at the landing swap. New LakesideSunDirection.ts
(lakesideSunForward(yawDeg), LAKESIDE_BOARD_YAW_DEG=0) is read by the board's
applyDir and by LakesideJourneyLighting with the journey lake's yaw (adapter
passes ()=>lakeYaw = L.yawDeg). The blend is unchanged: slerp from the captured
island rotation by w. lakesideModeLighting untouched.
Test: lakeside-journey-sun (w=1 journey sun == board sun in lake frame for yaw
180/90/0, old direction was mirrored, smooth slerp by w, wiring).
